INSERT INTO "reviews" ("id", "entity_type", "entity_id", "reviewer", "comment", "created_at", "resolved") VALUES (250, 'task', 'TASK-0070-00-00', 'MCP User', 'Committed d27457a on roadmap/r11-fields-and-freshness (not pushed). create_requirement warns on a missing acceptance_criteria, and on missing validation_metrics for NFUNC; create_task warns when a P0/P1 task has no test_plan. Routed through the R8 rules helper, so enforce refuses before any write and off is silent; warnings ride on the existing create results. Fields chosen from measured counts (validation_metrics 0/18, test_plan 12/69). The R10 shape test now passes a test_plan so it stays about shape. 349 passed (coverage 72.5%), lint clean, smoke 23 tools.', '2026-09-16 11:41:57', 0);
INSERT INTO "reviews" ("id", "entity_type", "entity_id", "reviewer", "comment", "created_at", "resolved") VALUES (251, 'task', 'TASK-0071-00-00', 'MCP User', 'Committed 52c89f5 on roadmap/r11-fields-and-freshness (not pushed). The server now answers prompts/list and prompts/get and offers capture_requirement: a guide the client''s own model fills in, taking what the person said as an optional argument, with no session kept on the server (F-08) and no cost to the tool budget (prompts are a separate primitive). The smoke script drives prompts/list over a real handshake: 23 tools, 1 prompt, clean stdout, fresh and on restart. 354 passed (coverage 72.6%), lint clean.', '2026-09-16 11:44:37', 0);
INSERT INTO "reviews" ("id", "entity_type", "entity_id", "reviewer", "comment", "created_at", "resolved") VALUES (252, 'task', 'TASK-0072-00-00', 'MCP User', 'Committed 452f5df on roadmap/r11-fields-and-freshness (not pushed). Requirement details show Last Verified, Never verified, or Stale since with the time content changed; the dashboard lists requirements not verified since their last change and counts them in the summary line, covering Draft ones too, skipping Deprecated. Derived from events and comments, no stored column. Second-resolution timestamps meant an edit and a check in the same second compared equal, so the verdict now uses lifecycle event ids (the ordering changes_since_review already trusts), with a same-second comment counting as a check. 359 passed (coverage 72.8%), lint clean, smoke 23 tools / 1 prompt.', '2026-09-16 11:49:35', 0);
INSERT INTO "reviews" ("id", "entity_type", "entity_id", "reviewer", "comment", "created_at", "resolved") VALUES (253, 'task', 'TASK-0073-00-00', 'MCP User', 'Committed bbb778b on roadmap/r11-fields-and-freshness (not pushed). 791 lines deleted: the requirement analysis, clarification and decomposition paths, the ADR diagram-suggestion paths, llm_decomposition_prompts.py, and the mcp_client plumbing through the server and both handler constructors. A script found the method boundaries by name and refused to cut anything still referenced, which caught that _create_single_requirement lives inside that run and had to stay; _create_requirement_dependency had no live caller and went. 359 passed, coverage up from 72.8% to 76.9%, lint clean, smoke 23 tools / 1 prompt.', '2026-09-16 11:52:38', 0);
INSERT INTO "reviews" ("id", "entity_type", "entity_id", "reviewer", "comment", "created_at", "resolved") VALUES (254, 'task', 'TASK-0074-00-00', 'MCP User', 'Committed c76b930 on roadmap/r11-fields-and-freshness (not pushed). README covers the capture prompt, thin-record warnings and the staleness signal; CLAUDE.md records that prompts carry no session and cost nothing against the tool budget, plus where the derivations live; CHANGELOG explains why the interview is not returning and lists the 791 removed lines. tests/test_r11_acceptance.py covers REQ-0006-FUNC-00''s six criteria, including a sweep proving no source file references mcp_client or sampling. CI command 365 passed (coverage 76.9%); default run incl. property tests 368 passed; lint clean; smoke 23 tools / 1 prompt.', '2026-09-16 11:56:06', 0);
